outputs.L1:
A method for producing a pre-insulated pipe, comprising:

- inserting a length of jacket pipe (10) into a guide channel (110) having a front end (111) and a rear end (112);
- securing the length of jacket pipe (10) within the guide channel (110);
- providing a first end (21) of a length of insulated inner piping (20), the insulated inner piping comprising a length of inner pipe surrounded by at least one layer of compressible insulation material (26);
- at the front end of the guide channel (110), inserting the first end (21) of the insulated inner piping (20) into the length of jacket pipe (10);
- applying an overpressure at least within the interior of the length of jacket pipe (10), around the inserted first end (21) of the insulated inner piping (20);
- moving the first end (21) of the insulated inner piping (20) toward the rear end (112) of the guide channel (110), wherein the overpressure is sufficient to radially compress the at least one layer of insulation material (26); and
- removing the overpressure to secure the length of insulated inner piping (20) within the length of jacket pipe (10), thereby forming a pre-insulated pipe.

counterfactuals.output:
1. **A method of manufacturing a pre-insulated pipe, the method comprising:**  
providing an inner piping assembly comprising an inner pipe surrounded by a radially compressible thermal-insulation layer;  
providing a jacket pipe having an internal passage with an internal transverse dimension smaller than an uncompressed external transverse dimension of the inner piping assembly;  
positioning a leading end of the inner piping assembly at an inlet of the jacket pipe;  
introducing pressurized fluid into the jacket pipe to establish an overpressure that exerts an insertion force on the inner piping assembly; and  
advancing the inner piping assembly through the internal passage by the insertion force while radially compressing the thermal-insulation layer against an inner surface of the jacket pipe, thereby forming the pre-insulated pipe.
